Law excerpts in data/rulebook are taken from official public sources listed in each record (source_url) and remain subject to
the terms of those sources. Client files in data/cases and cases/ are fictitious.
Relate is an open-source project of Neo4j (Apache-2.0); the viewer loads its WebAssembly build (@relate/relate-wasm) and
Cytoscape.js (MIT) from public CDNs. Casefold is not affiliated with or endorsed by Neo4j.

web/vendor/tesseract/ contains, unmodified, tesseract.js 5.1.1 and tesseract.js-core 5.1.1 (Apache-2.0, see the LICENSE files there) and
the "best_int" Dutch and English language data of Tesseract 4.0.0 (Apache-2.0, via @tesseract.js-data). The language data is
stored as base64 text (*.gz.b64.txt) so that static hosts that serve only common web types can serve it; web/vendor/tesseract/ocr-worker.js
decodes it. pdf.js (Apache-2.0) is loaded from cdnjs. The structure chart reader (web/chart.js, casefold/structure_chart.py) is
part of Casefold; casefold/structure_chart.py uses pdfplumber (MIT) when installed.
